---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: When the end-to-end tests run
    accDescr: A pull request runs the end-to-end tests only when it changes the app, its tests or their workflow; otherwise both required checks pass at once. The check nextcloud then runs every supported version, and the check nextcloud on PostgreSQL, MariaDB and S3 runs the newest version there when the change can behave differently on another database or storage, and the upgrade from the last release when the change can break it, and passes at once otherwise. Every push to main and every night run both, and every Monday the canary runs the tests against the coming Nextcloud. The contract tests run the app against a real Paperless-ngx 2.x and 3.x every Monday, by hand, and in a pull request that changes how the app talks to Paperless.

    pr["Pull request"]
    main["Push to main,<br>every night,<br>by hand"]
    affected{"affected.sh:<br>can the change<br>affect the app?"}
    all["nextcloud:<br>every supported<br>version side by side"]
    variants["nextcloud on<br>PostgreSQL, MariaDB<br>and S3: the<br>newest version, and<br>the upgrade from<br>the last release"]
    skipped["both checks<br>pass in seconds"]
    result["passed<br>or failed"]
    monday["Every Monday,<br>by hand"]
    canary["canary.sh:<br>the coming Nextcloud"]
    contract["run-contract.sh:<br>Paperless-ngx<br>2.x and 3.x"]

    pr --> affected
    affected -- "lib/, appinfo/,<br>templates/, js/,<br>css/, l10n/, img/,<br>composer.json,<br>tests/e2e/, e2e.yml" --> all
    affected -- "the migrations,<br>the state, the storage,<br>the uploads, the settings,<br>the package, info.xml,<br>tests/e2e/, e2e.yml" --> variants
    affected -- "documentation,<br>other workflows,<br>the version<br>of a release" --> skipped
    main --> all
    main --> variants
    %% Invisible links keep the triggers in one row and the canary below the rest.
    main ~~~ affected
    all --> result
    variants --> result
    result ~~~ monday
    monday --> canary
    monday --> contract
    affected -- "E2E_QUESTION=contract:<br>the client of Paperless,<br>the mock, the fixtures,<br>the contract tests" --> contract

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class pr person
    class affected,all,variants,canary,contract bot
    class skipped,result done
